    "['ip address [ip-address] [subnet-mask]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.2/24', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Huawei \"ip address\" configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.2/24\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. The interface naming follows a different convention (ge-x/y/z instead of GigabitEthernet)\\n2. We explicitly specify the unit number (typically 0 for physical interfaces)\\n3. The subnet is specified in CIDR notation (/24 instead of 255.255.255.0)\\n4. The address family (inet for IPv4) must be explicitly declared', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.2/24'}]]": 1,
